MID_EV12_051_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_051_m01_001: Hello there, brave participants in the Heroic Games!\nTime for an Anna administrative announcement!
MID_EV12_051_m01_002: But first, let me congratulate you on defeating Cetus,\nthe Sea Tyrant. Incredible work!
MID_EV12_051_m01_003: Incredible? You bet we were! Cetus was huge—\nand fast!
MID_EV12_051_m01_004: And what a ship we rode in on! My compliments to\nDagda the Great.
MID_EV12_051_m01_005: We couldn't have done it otherwise—Cetus would\nhave smashed us to bits.
MID_EV12_051_m01_006: Now we're back, and we're safe. And...I'm glad\nabout how it all turned out.
MID_EV12_051_m01_007: Looks like there's a story to tell, indeed. I sense a\nchange in you.
MID_EV12_051_m01_008: I think you've grown up a little bit.
MID_EV12_051_m01_009: Hm, really? I guess I'll take that as a compliment.
MID_EV12_051_m01_010: Of course it is! It's good that people see it.
MID_EV12_051_m01_011: We can't forget that your next match is coming up.\nThe main matches are all on the schedule.
MID_EV12_051_m01_012: And that's why I'm here today, House Lamine! It's\nalmost time.
MID_EV12_051_m01_013: Since you were all so busy, I thought you might need\na little reminder.
MID_EV12_051_m01_014: <TLP>Match: First Main Match of the Heroic Games\nOpponent: Bridal Party of the Pale Raven\n\nDate: {DateTime=Month} {DateTime=Day}
MID_EV12_051_m01_015: This? I am aware.
MID_EV12_051_m01_016: The schedule has been announced to the public\nalready. Our opponent is to be Anatolia.
MID_EV12_051_m01_017: Well, there you go! You're absolutely right.
MID_EV12_051_m01_018: Hmhmhm... How fortunate that our first opponent is\nthe one I am fated to meet.
MID_EV12_051_m01_019: I may not put much stock in it, but I do wonder if\nthis is the hand of providence at work.
MID_EV12_051_m01_020: Hey, Fabio? If you want to keep up the priest act,\nmaybe...don't say that kind of thing out loud.
MID_EV12_051_m01_021: If Anatolia is to be our opponent, I can look forward\nto a fine duel.
MID_EV12_051_m01_022: There isn't much time—use it to make sure\nyou're ready!
MID_EV12_051_m01_023: She's right. We don't have the time for another big\nadventure before the fight.
MID_EV12_051_m01_024: Good point. We should just stay in Dagsion. We\nneed to be ready!
MID_EV12_051_m01_025: Very well. I do have a task that I can no longer\nignore. So I shall not.
MID_EV12_051_m01_026: It is an order from Vritra, after all.
MID_EV12_051_m01_027: 
MID_EV12_052_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_052_m01_001: How rare. You are unafraid.
MID_EV12_052_m01_002: Look! Sweetie's found a cat! He said they usually\nrun away.
MID_EV12_052_m01_003: How nice! He finally made a feline friend.
MID_EV12_052_m01_004: Mikaela, is it me, or is something different about\nSweetie these days?
MID_EV12_052_m01_005: I don't think he even realizes it himself.
MID_EV12_052_m01_006: Sure that's not just wishful thinking?
MID_EV12_052_m01_007: No way! And this is the proof—that cat came right\nup to him!
MID_EV12_052_m01_008: This place is so starkly different from the village of\nKunlun, is it not?
MID_EV12_052_m01_009: People, water, plants, animals... All things Kunlun\nlacks; all things Dagsion has in abundance.
MID_EV12_052_m01_010: My enmity toward the gods is undiminished, but I \nfrankly admire this metropolis, in all its grandeur.
MID_EV12_052_m01_011: It is extraordinary. It accepts and contains all that\nthere is.
MID_EV12_052_m01_012: Turning to our journey... You were not able to obtain\nwhat you sought.
MID_EV12_052_m01_013: Indeed. But it was not time wasted, I feel.
MID_EV12_052_m01_014: <NCA>Inquire.
MID_EV12_052_m01_015: <NCB>Leave it.
MID_EV12_052_m01_016: <ACA>Hm. Explain.
MID_EV12_052_m01_017: <ACA>No one could be more surprised by this than I, but\nI have come to enjoy our travels together.
MID_EV12_052_m01_018: <ACA>Trekking across this land and delving into its\nmysteries is a delight.
MID_EV12_052_m01_019: <ACB>Hm.
MID_EV12_052_m01_020: Till now, I had thought of you all as little more than\nvermin infesting the surface.
MID_EV12_052_m01_021: I know not when, but my thinking began to change.
MID_EV12_052_m01_022: It is not only you, Dietrich. Esmeralda and\nMikaela too.
MID_EV12_052_m01_023: I find it curious, but your companionship brings\nme ease.
MID_EV12_052_m01_024: You once said that the difference between beasts and\nhumans is that beasts live by instinct alone.
MID_EV12_052_m01_025: So you recall my words. But—
MID_EV12_052_m01_026: Driven by instinct, living and dying in battle...
MID_EV12_052_m01_027: If, rather than a human, I am judged to be no more\nthan a beast, I feel no shame.
MID_EV12_052_m01_028: It may even be that I have striven for this with the\nwhole of my being.
MID_EV12_052_m01_029: Like Hedda, the warrior who at the end of her\nbattles became Cetus, the Sea Tyrant.
MID_EV12_052_m01_030: Ah!
MID_EV12_052_m01_031: In the end, I am but a demon that leaves a trail\nof carnage.
MID_EV12_052_m01_032: The euphoria I feel battling the strong is my\nsustenance. Perhaps this is the curse of my blood.
MID_EV12_052_m01_033: Yet I do not rebuke my ancestors. And I will\nnot today.
MID_EV12_052_m01_034: I see. Perhaps it is alright then.
MID_EV12_105_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_105_m01_001: Hm?
MID_EV12_105_m01_002: You escaped me before, but today, I claim your\nHeart Core.
MID_EV12_105_m01_003: Your time has come, Periandros.
MID_EV12_105_m01_004: Agh!
MID_EV12_105_m01_005: Borrowing someone else's toy without permission is\nrude. Breaking it? Unforgivable.
MID_EV12_105_m01_006: If someone is going to break him, it can only be me.\nDon't you agree, Babbu?
MID_EV12_105_m01_007: I had intuited that you are far from ordinary, but it\nappears you are in fact a child of the goddess.
MID_EV12_105_m01_008: Periandros! You allowed our sworn foe to steal your\nheart and abandoned your duty. You are unworthy!
MID_EV12_105_m01_009: I think you may be too busy for a chat. Look lively!
MID_EV12_105_m01_010: Urk...
MID_EV12_105_m01_011: There's not much to you, is there? Oh well. I'll be\nbreaking you now.
MID_EV12_105_m01_012: Hah!
MID_EV12_105_m01_013: My sister has spoken of you... Why are you here?
MID_EV12_105_m01_014: Dietrich! How did you find me?
MID_EV12_105_m01_015: Go. Now.
MID_EV12_105_m01_016: You two! Stop at once!
MID_EV12_105_m01_017: Neither Lyrah's kiss nor Father's remains had an\neffect on him. Troubling...
MID_EV12_105_m01_018: I am wracked with guilt, Lady Iliana, that you would\nbe forced to compensate for my weakness.
MID_EV12_105_m01_019: It was no trouble. I would hate to see someone else\nsteal you away from me.
MID_EV12_105_m01_020: I have spent so many days cozying up to Solel. Lying\nto him. Soon, our plan will come to pass.
MID_EV12_105_m01_021: Do you know how infuriating it is? To have him call\nme a name that is not mine, but hers?
MID_EV12_105_m01_022: But you, Yanjin...
MID_EV12_105_m01_023: I know that you're all mine. There's not a drop of\nyou that isn't...
MID_EV12_105_m01_024: You are the only one that I adore. Aside from Father,\nof course...there is just you.
MID_EV12_105_m01_025: Oh! Lady Iliana! Never has there been a soul more\nfortunate than I!
MID_EV12_105_m01_026: Devote yourself to me, Yanjin... Until the flame in\nyour furnace is extinguished.
MID_EV12_105_m01_027: Rgh... *cough*
MID_EV12_105_m01_028: You hurt, don't you? We'll have to find some way to\nfix that Heart Core of yours. It is unique.
MID_EV12_105_m01_029: Quite a surprise to be rescued by you. Why?
MID_EV12_105_m01_030: I would find it inconvenient if you were to die.
MID_EV12_105_m01_031: I am now certain. Being with you does bring\nme ease.
MID_EV12_105_m01_032: To think it took this long to understand... But finally,\nI do.
MID_EV12_105_m01_033: My mission, and the friction between gods and\nmankind... It all feels so trivial.
MID_EV12_105_m01_034: You have diverted me far from my path. What a\ntroublemaker you are.
MID_EV12_053_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_053_m01_001: I see. You are different than before.
MID_EV12_053_m01_002: You found something on your journey. You are now\nredolent of the scent of strength.
MID_EV12_053_m01_003: I gained much, and I lost much. It was an exchange.
MID_EV12_053_m01_004: At this moment, I am here only to defeat you in order\nto fulfill my mission.
MID_EV12_053_m01_005: It is good to see you again, Mediator of Nuwa—as I\nsuspect you must be.
MID_EV12_053_m01_006: How would you know such things?
MID_EV12_053_m01_007: We visited the village of Kunlun. I know its secrets.
MID_EV12_053_m01_008: You see, I set foot in this land entrusted with a\ncritical mission.
MID_EV12_053_m01_009: Do you shoulder an equally important burden?
MID_EV12_053_m01_010: What drives you forward? And when you reach your\ngoal, how might that affect the world?
MID_EV12_053_m01_011: Have you considered every factor? Have you truly\nunderstood the impact of your duty?
MID_EV12_053_m01_012: Or are you thoughtlessly fulfilling the role that you\nwere given, and no more than that?
MID_EV12_053_m01_013: Why are you asking me these questions?
MID_EV12_053_m01_014: Why is he talking to her like that? Why is he being\nso mean?
MID_EV12_053_m01_015: I'm sure they could just talk things over. Wouldn't\nthat be easier?
MID_EV12_053_m01_016: Maybe he's trying to rile her up.
MID_EV12_053_m01_017: If your foe sees red, they won't be thinking straight\nduring the fight. It's an old trick.
MID_EV12_053_m01_018: I'm not so sure about that. I think he's just rude.
MID_EV12_053_m01_019: It seems we have no common ground. A pity.
MID_EV12_053_m01_020: Perhaps we should simply settle things as the\nDagdans do—in battle.
MID_EV12_053_m01_021: If I win, the Grand Megaliths are mine to command.\nIf you win, I will forget Kunlun.
MID_EV12_053_m01_022: If you are so hurried to face defeat, I'll gladly accept\nyour conditions.
MID_EV12_053_m01_023: These missions, these opposing factions, the future\nitself...
MID_EV12_053_m01_024: Scraps for the dogs. Irrelevant.
MID_EV12_053_m01_025: How dare you speak about our mission like that!
MID_EV12_053_m01_026: As battle rages, to burn blindingly for a\nsingle instant...
MID_EV12_053_m01_027: That is what I long for. That is my joy. That is\nmy meaning.
MID_EV12_053_m01_028: Ugh, I don't know what he's talking about anymore.\nHe's got such a bloated sense of self...
MID_EV12_053_m01_029: I finally see you clearly, Dietrich. You are a very\ndangerous person.
MID_EV12_053_m01_030: Ahahaha! You are far from the first to say so.\nAll that is left is to dance! To revel!
MID_EV12_054_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_054_m01_030: Oh...
MID_EV12_054_m01_001: We are victorious.
MID_EV12_054_m01_002: Ngh...
MID_EV12_054_m01_003: A decisive loss. Regrettable.
MID_EV12_054_m01_004: I will not report the existence of Nuwa to Vritra. You\nhave my word.
MID_EV12_054_m01_005: Rest assured, the people of Kunlun are safe. They\nwere not welcoming, but I won't hold it against them.
MID_EV12_054_m01_006: Let us just say that I understand why you fear Vritra.
MID_EV12_054_m01_007: I appreciate your follow-through. But will you\nbe alright?
MID_EV12_054_m01_008: A strange question. Of course not. If this becomes\nknown to Agartha, I will be branded a traitor.
MID_EV12_054_m01_009: But perhaps I have broiled in the sunlight of this land\ntoo long. It is, as ever, detestable.
MID_EV12_054_m01_010: When I asked you of your mission, of your\nconviction, those questions were not only for you.
MID_EV12_054_m01_011: I have lived a long life of service to Agartha, and\naccomplished much.
MID_EV12_054_m01_012: But I begin to harbor doubts, and to ponder what\nall this was for.
MID_EV12_054_m01_013: And I wonder if serving an inscrutable machine is a\nmission of value.
MID_EV12_054_m01_014: My own mission is to protect everyone in Kunlun.
MID_EV12_054_m01_015: When I close my eyes, I can see their faces—the lives\nof those I must protect.
MID_EV12_054_m01_016: They have been so kind to me. Which is one of the\nmany reasons I want to save them.
MID_EV12_054_m01_017: There is sense in what you say. And perhaps your\nvery nature does not leave room to harbor doubts.
MID_EV12_054_m01_018: Incidentally, I met another who used the same magic\nas you in Dagsion. A man named Yanjin.
MID_EV12_054_m01_019: Ah, yes. I have encountered him too. Periandros is\nhis true name.
MID_EV12_054_m01_020: Could he be Periandros? The one I seek?
MID_EV12_054_m01_021: He has deserted us. I was tasked with locating him.
MID_EV12_054_m01_022: Our Heart Cores supply us with enduring power.\nBut the technology to construct them is lost.
MID_EV12_054_m01_023: The one he possesses is special. Unique, in fact.\nAgartha is desperate to regain it.
MID_EV12_054_m01_024: But it seems he is now devoted to another, in\nthis land.
MID_EV12_054_m01_025: I believe I may understand him...a little.
MID_EV12_054_m01_026: Ultimately, I may well share his fate. To be hunted as\na betrayer... 
MID_EV12_054_m01_027: Strange to say it, but I have begun to accept the idea.
MID_EV12_054_m01_028: Anacharsis. You seem to me a very strong person.
MID_EV12_054_m01_029: Please, call me Fabio. I have become quite attached\nto this name.